==Strategy==
Cat Trial is a stage where the enemy is playing defensively, and is notable for being one of the first SoL stages where the enemy's defensive ability is the primary source of difficulty. To test the player's offensive potential, this level sends out One Horns as heavy barriers; each one has a massive health pool and will respawn quickly after death. However, if you manage to kill one of the One Horns, you obtain a large sum of money, which you can use to your advantage by sending out all of your units. It is important not to waste that money, so units like [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]] should be avoided, in favor of defensive units or strong attackers.

There are a few ways to approach this stage:

#'''Holding the line''': Attempt to build a stack of [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]] (such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]]) while spamming meatshields. When the One Horns die, quickly send out [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Holy Valkyrie]] to hopefully freeze Camelle, then send in attackers to deal some damage before being forced to repeat the process. Alternatively, just send in attackers.
#'''Luring''': Simply stall the One Horns near the Cat Base and try to kill them all at once or close to it. After that, start whaling on Camelle with rushers like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|A. Bahamut]] or tanky attackers like [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island]] and [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera]] variants to kill him before the second wave. This should be possible with just A. Bahamut and meatshields even in 2-crown difficulty.
#'''Piercing''': Build up a line of defence, but try to use the One Horns as a stepping stone to kill Camelle with [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]]/[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion]] units. Notably good units for this are certain specific [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Ubers]] and [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]], with [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]] and/or [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe]] defending. There are also many options in {{4c}}, such as [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Mina]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]], [[Adult Cat (Rare Cat)|Prisoner]] or [[Talents|Talented]] [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]].

